WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.373
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.473 --> 00:02.328
I want to...

3
00:03.545 --> 00:05.663
do couple-like things

4
00:08.008 --> 00:10.103
with you, too, Ryosuke.

5
00:18.086 --> 00:20.255
So?

6
00:20.255 --> 00:22.502
How far do couple things go?

7
00:22.502 --> 00:26.395
Huh? What do you mean, how far?

8
00:40.318 --> 00:43.393
Tell me. Hurry.

9
01:33.103 --> 01:35.176
Ryosuke?

10
02:26.021 --> 02:27.388
Huh?

11
02:33.886 --> 02:35.173
What the...

12
02:42.886 --> 02:44.458
Oh, good morning.

13
02:45.217 --> 02:46.684
Good morning.

14
02:48.884 --> 02:52.319
Oh, right. Are you okay?

15
02:52.319 --> 02:56.316
You drank quite a lot last night. Are you feeling sick at all?

16
02:58.762 --> 03:00.264
Yeah...

17
03:02.248 --> 03:03.875
Wow, I'm sorry...

18
03:04.893 --> 03:06.593
I'm really sorry...

19
03:08.731 --> 03:11.472
Do you remember what happened yesterday?

20
03:11.472 --> 03:13.013
I...

21
03:14.393 --> 03:15.893
I remember.

22
03:29.557 --> 03:31.694
Did I scare you?

23
03:36.999 --> 03:38.652
No, you didn't.

24
03:44.871 --> 03:46.833
That's a relief.

25
04:06.731 --> 04:08.651
Are you hungry?

26
04:08.651 --> 04:11.121
Yeah, a little.

27
04:13.963 --> 04:16.371
Then let's eat.

28
04:16.371 --> 04:17.871
Sounds good.

29
04:28.094 --> 04:30.085
I used your shower.

30
04:34.581 --> 04:38.688
Wow, this looks really delicious.

31
04:39.988 --> 04:41.392
Is tea okay?

32
04:42.407 --> 04:43.575
Yeah.

33
04:47.836 --> 04:49.977
- It's good. - Really?

34
04:49.977 --> 04:51.550
I'm glad.

35
04:52.578 --> 04:54.177
You cook, huh?

36
04:54.177 --> 04:56.857
Yeah, just a little.

37
05:05.965 --> 05:07.755
This is nice.

38
05:09.539 --> 05:12.217
Having you here when I wake up.

39
05:16.070 --> 05:17.370
Yeah.

40
05:18.202 --> 05:20.356
What do you mean, "Yeah"?

41
05:21.984 --> 05:25.437
It's just... I'm happy, too.

42
05:26.037 --> 05:27.604
You're happy?

43
05:28.328 --> 05:29.830
Yeah.

44
05:29.830 --> 05:31.233
What made you happy?

45
05:31.233 --> 05:33.324
- Specifically? - Yeah.

46
05:34.283 --> 05:35.623
Everything.

47
05:35.623 --> 05:36.995
Everything?

48
05:38.881 --> 05:40.851
Tell me in detail.

49
05:43.494 --> 05:46.195
This moment. This time right now.

50
05:47.415 --> 05:48.981
I see.

51
05:56.985 --> 06:00.158
Wait, Taguchi?

52
06:01.580 --> 06:03.042
Ryo...

53
06:04.905 --> 06:06.588
...suke.

54
06:07.626 --> 06:12.183
You're a little too close.

55
06:14.105 --> 06:16.479
Are you heading home?

56
06:16.479 --> 06:20.187
Yeah. I need to change before going to work.

57
06:22.933 --> 06:24.713
I see.

58
06:29.640 --> 06:31.995
I don't wanna let you go.

59
06:44.491 --> 06:46.078
Just kidding.

60
07:12.407 --> 07:19.208
Did we manage to do at least one couple thing?

61
07:25.916 --> 07:27.338
I'm sorry...

62
07:28.758 --> 07:32.764
Sorry, wait a second.

63
07:36.879 --> 07:39.252
If we go further, I won't stop.

64
08:03.358 --> 08:06.211
Shiori, you're the best girlfriend ever.

65
08:09.077 --> 08:12.193
And you, Ryosuke,

66
08:12.193 --> 08:16.291
are the best boyfriend.

67
08:32.410 --> 08:33.722
Are you good on time?

68
08:33.722 --> 08:35.963
Yeah, I should be fine.

69
08:35.963 --> 08:37.976
See you at work.

70
08:37.976 --> 08:39.072
Okay.

71
09:43.522 --> 09:46.091
We'll go ahead with this then.

72
09:46.091 --> 09:49.006
Thank you. I'll take care of it.

73
09:49.625 --> 09:52.609
Mr. Kashiwagi! I compiled the test data.

74
09:52.609 --> 09:55.174
Wow, that was fast. I'm impressed.

75
09:55.174 --> 09:59.105
Because you said you wanted it as soon as possible, Mr. Kashiwagi.

76
09:59.105 --> 10:03.346
Sorry about that. Seriously, this helps a lot. Thank you.

77
10:05.365 --> 10:09.215
His communication skills are amazing.

78
10:12.390 --> 10:13.940
They really are.

79
10:13.940 --> 10:16.933
It's hard to believe he's only been here a week.

80
10:21.062 --> 10:22.791
Come in.

81
10:22.791 --> 10:24.124
Excuse me. I'm coming in.

82
10:24.124 --> 10:26.204
Good work.

83
10:28.363 --> 10:29.336
Hello there.

84
10:29.336 --> 10:30.540
Good work.

85
10:30.540 --> 10:32.349
- Hello. - Hi.

86
10:33.899 --> 10:35.633
Sorry for taking up your time.

87
10:35.633 --> 10:36.860
- Not at all. - It's fine.

88
10:36.860 --> 10:39.993
I want to talk about the school for the field test.

89
10:39.993 --> 10:43.622
This is your Alma mater, right?

90
10:43.622 --> 10:47.204
Could you two go together to say hello before the test begins?

91
10:49.041 --> 10:50.138
Understood.

92
10:50.138 --> 10:51.283
- Sure. - Glad to hear that.

93
10:51.283 --> 10:53.921
The head of one of the grades is our point person.

94
10:53.921 --> 10:55.738
You have their contact info, right?

95
10:55.738 --> 10:56.848
Yes.

96
10:56.848 --> 11:00.117
[Kanagawa Prefectural Tsurushiro High School]

97
11:10.815 --> 11:13.235
Sorry! Did you wait long?

98
11:13.235 --> 11:15.308
No, not at all.

99
11:15.308 --> 11:17.161
- Let's go. - Okay.

100
11:22.646 --> 11:24.160
You're going to Tsurushiro?

101
11:24.160 --> 11:28.430
Yeah, I'm heading to a meeting with Kashiwagi.

102
11:29.391 --> 11:32.505
I think you'll join us when the field test starts,

103
11:32.505 --> 11:34.998
so let's do our best, okay?

104
11:37.155 --> 11:38.313
Sure.

105
11:40.985 --> 11:43.394
Remember your last client?

106
11:43.394 --> 11:45.339
Yes, I remember.

107
11:45.339 --> 11:48.959
We're trying to start another project there.

108
11:48.959 --> 11:51.357
We want you to come, Taguchi.

109
11:54.617 --> 11:56.394
You see...

110
11:56.394 --> 11:57.634
Yeah?

111
11:59.905 --> 12:04.223
I mean, who's our point person at the school?

112
12:04.223 --> 12:07.396
It's Mr. Nomoto. He's the head teacher for one of the grades now.

113
12:07.396 --> 12:08.956
Oh, the guidance counselor?

114
12:08.956 --> 12:10.163
Yep.

115
12:11.563 --> 12:13.302
How old is he now?

116
12:13.302 --> 12:15.360
Well, not sure.

117
12:15.360 --> 12:17.409
Maybe in his fifties?

118
12:17.409 --> 12:19.396
Probably around that age.

119
12:24.994 --> 12:27.037
It's been a while.

120
12:28.626 --> 12:30.616
I'm doing well.

121
12:33.476 --> 12:35.698
How do you still remember that?

122
12:35.698 --> 12:38.549
Please forget it...

123
12:41.970 --> 12:43.774
Yes.

124
12:43.774 --> 12:47.281
She's here. Do you want to speak to her?

125
12:48.977 --> 12:50.495
It's Mr. Nomoto.

126
12:53.755 --> 12:55.493
Hello?

127
12:56.751 --> 13:00.049
Yes, this is Yamane. It's been a long time.

128
13:02.407 --> 13:07.543
Yes, that's right. It really is a coincidence. Yes.

129
13:08.615 --> 13:11.277
I'm really looking forward to it too.

130
13:13.075 --> 13:17.961
Yes, I look forward to seeing you. Thank you.

131
13:22.201 --> 13:25.755
[Can we head home together today?]

132
13:36.663 --> 13:38.003
Hey there.

133
13:38.683 --> 13:40.050
Hi.

134
13:50.003 --> 13:52.463
Were you okay that night?

135
13:52.463 --> 13:55.187
I had a terrible hangover after that.

136
13:56.194 --> 13:57.684
Oh, really?

137
14:06.103 --> 14:07.639
[I'm not sure yet.]

138
14:07.639 --> 14:11.443
[If I don't have to work overtime, I wanna go home with you!]

139
14:20.061 --> 14:21.609
Is it Ms. Yamane?

140
14:24.204 --> 14:25.424
Yeah.

141
14:27.145 --> 14:29.009
Do you go home together?

142
14:30.450 --> 14:33.028
Only when our timing lines up.

143
14:33.028 --> 14:35.150
I see.

144
14:35.150 --> 14:39.256
Wow, I never thought I'd see you make that face.

145
14:40.408 --> 14:43.103
I couldn't have imagined this in high school.

146
14:52.935 --> 14:55.273
After you transferred schools,

147
14:56.150 --> 14:59.662
Ms. Yamane was really depressed.

148
15:03.820 --> 15:08.245
Well, I was just worried about her from afar.

149
15:14.347 --> 15:15.694
Bye then.

150
15:19.680 --> 15:23.773
Hello. This is Kashiwagi from Meigakusha.

151
15:23.773 --> 15:26.667
Yes, thank you for calling back.

152
15:30.207 --> 15:32.495
That's why this sucks.

153
15:36.453 --> 15:43.369
We'll share the schedule we have now with the development team and...

154
15:43.369 --> 15:46.372
Ms. Yamane, you can stop here for today.

155
15:46.372 --> 15:48.139
Wait, but...

156
15:48.139 --> 15:50.503
Don't you have plans with Taguchi?

157
15:50.503 --> 15:51.429
Huh?

158
15:51.429 --> 15:54.619
I'll head home right after I finish this part.

159
15:56.130 --> 15:57.517
Good work.

160
16:00.313 --> 16:02.228
Good work.

161
16:27.963 --> 16:29.130
You're here.

162
16:29.130 --> 16:31.088
Hey there.

163
16:31.088 --> 16:32.715
Let's go.

164
16:32.715 --> 16:34.022
Okay.

165
16:42.782 --> 16:45.172
What should we do for dinner?

166
16:45.172 --> 16:46.552
Oh...

167
16:51.677 --> 16:54.850
It's pretty late.

168
16:54.850 --> 16:57.310
Wanna stop by a restaurant?

169
17:11.748 --> 17:14.979
You seem happy today, Yamane.

170
17:14.979 --> 17:16.906
Did something good happen?

171
17:18.005 --> 17:22.784
Well, there's something I'm kind of looking forward to after this.

172
17:22.784 --> 17:27.467
Well, there's hardly any work left, so you can go home for today.

173
17:28.682 --> 17:33.554
Thank you! Then I'll head out first.

174
17:33.554 --> 17:35.541
See you.

175
17:36.837 --> 17:38.661
Huh?

176
17:38.661 --> 17:40.503
Is something wrong?

177
17:40.503 --> 17:44.331
The book title and barcode info don't match.

178
17:44.331 --> 17:47.013
Maybe they were stuck on the wrong data.

179
17:47.013 --> 17:51.700
Probably. A bunch of books came in at once the other day.

180
17:51.700 --> 17:55.308
We'll need to redo them all.

181
17:55.308 --> 17:57.227
I'll do it.

182
17:57.227 --> 17:58.440
You will?

183
17:58.440 --> 18:01.339
I don't have practice today, so I'm free.

184
18:03.792 --> 18:06.402
Yamane, see you.

185
18:15.551 --> 18:17.058
Wait...

186
18:21.316 --> 18:23.524
Kashiwagi!

187
18:23.524 --> 18:25.651
You're still here!

188
18:26.499 --> 18:28.921
Didn't you have plans with Taguchi?

189
18:28.921 --> 18:31.116
I told him to go on ahead today.

190
18:31.116 --> 18:35.473
This report is due today, right? I'll help you finish it.

191
18:49.354 --> 18:50.461
Yamane!

192
18:50.461 --> 18:52.907
At first, I thought you were a quiet girl.

193
18:52.907 --> 18:55.504
Here's this month's library newsletter.

194
18:55.504 --> 18:59.019
Ms. Kawatani wants it on the bulletin board.

195
18:59.019 --> 19:01.050
Thank you.

196
19:03.048 --> 19:04.495
That's why...

197
19:05.541 --> 19:07.734
Yamane! Good morning.

198
19:07.734 --> 19:09.882
Good morning.

199
19:09.882 --> 19:12.212
It's like I was overstepping.

200
19:12.212 --> 19:13.734
Yamane!

201
19:14.619 --> 19:16.004
Good work!

202
19:16.004 --> 19:18.057
- Good work. - Every time I saw Yamane,

203
19:18.057 --> 19:19.785
- PE lesson? - I'd call out to her.

204
19:19.785 --> 19:20.966
Yeah.

205
19:21.968 --> 19:24.263
- But... - Wait!

206
19:26.404 --> 19:28.792
I'll help too.

207
19:28.792 --> 19:31.898
It'll get done faster with more people.

208
19:31.898 --> 19:34.846
Really? Sorry, thank you.

209
19:34.846 --> 19:37.938
Yamane doesn't need me looking out for her.

210
19:37.938 --> 19:41.166
I'll check the shelves over there.

211
19:41.166 --> 19:43.945
She can think and act for herself.

212
19:43.945 --> 19:47.026
I'll start from the other side.

213
19:47.026 --> 19:48.739
Thank you.

214
19:50.463 --> 19:55.015
I realized how presumptuous I was, thinking I had to check in on her.

215
19:56.490 --> 19:58.515
It felt arrogant.

216
20:15.678 --> 20:18.919
I'm heading over there. See you at school.

217
20:18.919 --> 20:20.292
Okay.

218
20:20.292 --> 20:21.752
Bye.

219
20:24.469 --> 20:28.515
Honestly, they were an unexpected pair.

220
20:29.181 --> 20:32.188
I'll take it. How much?

221
20:32.188 --> 20:34.318
No, it's fine.

222
20:34.318 --> 20:35.320
Here.

223
20:39.239 --> 20:40.812
Thank you.

224
20:47.193 --> 20:50.958
So, is that all?

225
20:50.958 --> 20:52.418
Yeah.

226
20:52.418 --> 20:54.352
Bye, then.

227
20:56.213 --> 21:00.223
Taguchi! Thanks for this.

228
21:00.223 --> 21:01.476
Sure.

229
21:11.106 --> 21:14.383
Are we having an after-party after the culture fest?

230
21:14.383 --> 21:16.571
Of course we are.

231
21:16.571 --> 21:17.757
Huh? Aren't we?

232
21:17.757 --> 21:21.075
I was wondering how long we'd stay.

233
21:21.075 --> 21:22.771
Everyone's going.

234
21:22.771 --> 21:26.935
But honestly, won't it feel awkward inviting Taguchi?

235
21:28.038 --> 21:30.055
Yeah, that's true.

236
21:30.887 --> 21:33.633
He's good-looking, though.

237
21:35.002 --> 21:37.691
He seems like a nice guy.

238
21:37.691 --> 21:38.918
Huh?

239
21:38.918 --> 21:42.288
I heard he's close with Yamane.

240
21:43.319 --> 21:45.045
Yamane?

241
21:45.045 --> 21:48.930
From Class 4. They're both library committee members.

242
21:51.172 --> 21:53.314
Wait, he's Yamane's type?

243
21:53.314 --> 21:54.626
What do you mean?

244
21:54.626 --> 21:55.922
Well...

245
21:57.371 --> 21:59.890
Pass me the red pen. Red pen.

246
21:59.890 --> 22:02.417
- Red? - Here.

247
22:02.417 --> 22:04.283
- Here you go. - Thanks.

248
22:05.659 --> 22:09.806
From that casual single line...

249
22:10.622 --> 22:12.222
Taguchi?

250
22:13.601 --> 22:18.774
I never imagined it would turn out like this...

251
22:20.465 --> 22:22.558
I never saw it coming.

252
22:24.118 --> 22:26.646
So did Taguchi drop out in the end?

253
22:26.646 --> 22:29.534
No, he didn't drop out. He transferred.

254
22:29.534 --> 22:31.238
Really?

255
22:31.238 --> 22:33.198
Why?

256
22:33.198 --> 22:34.918
No clue.

257
22:49.953 --> 22:51.607
Gosh...

258
22:52.995 --> 22:54.578
I...

259
22:54.578 --> 22:56.657
See you at school.

260
22:56.657 --> 22:58.103
Okay.

261
22:58.103 --> 23:01.882
- Bye. - I was in love.

262
23:01.882 --> 23:03.769
With Yamane.

263
23:13.232 --> 23:14.799
Hey...

264
23:21.921 --> 23:24.142
I can say this now, but...

265
23:27.147 --> 23:28.554
I...

266
23:30.447 --> 23:33.370
Mr. Taguchi is leaving the project.

267
23:33.370 --> 23:34.553
What?

268
23:34.553 --> 23:37.206
Shiori, don't worry about it.

269
23:37.206 --> 23:38.960
Did something happen with him?

270
23:38.960 --> 23:43.456
It's easier to speak your true feelings if you feel loved.

271
23:43.456 --> 23:45.144
Did you date before?

272
23:45.144 --> 23:46.590
No.

273
23:46.590 --> 23:49.036
Don't talk to me anymore.

274
23:49.036 --> 23:51.118
Putting distance between you again...

275
23:51.118 --> 23:53.557
Are you gonna regret it for years again?

276
23:53.557 --> 23:59.929
I wonder if Ryosuke is being honest with his own feelings.
